## 3.8 Classification

### Purpose

The Classification section records the engineering classification of a System Objective within the approved AVIA objective taxonomy.

Its purpose is to ensure that every objective is consistently organized, searchable, and managed according to its primary engineering purpose.

---

### Standard Fields

Every System Objective shall include the following fields:

| Field | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| Primary Category | The approved engineering category to which the objective belongs. |
| Secondary Classification | Additional approved classification, where applicable. |
| Engineering Domain | The engineering domain impacted by the objective. |
| Classification Justification | Explanation supporting the assigned classification. |

---

### Classification Rules

The classification shall:

- Assign exactly one primary category.
- Use only approved engineering categories.
- Be supported by documented engineering justification.
- Remain consistent with the Objective Governance framework.
- Be reviewed whenever the objective undergoes significant engineering revision.

---

### Engineering Note

Classification supports repository organization and engineering navigation.

It does not alter the meaning, authority, or identity of the objective.
